#!/usr/bin/python3
# =============================================================================
# nimbus-update — NimbusOS update tool
# =============================================================================
# What: one place for all update logic on an installed NimbusOS system:
#         status    what is installed, which channel and policy, last check
#         check     refresh package lists, explain any failure, list pending
#                   updates (Security / NimbusOS / Debian), fetch the signed
#                   release notes, write /var/lib/nimbusos/update-status.json
#         install   apt-get update + full-upgrade, non-interactive, keeping
#                   local configuration files (used by "Install updates")
#         auto      the "Automatic" policy: upgrade NimbusOS's own packages,
#                   pulling in new dependencies (nimbus-update-auto.timer)
#         channel   switch between the stable and beta channels
#         policy    automatic | notify | off
#         history   past apt runs, parsed from /var/log/apt/history.log
#       --json makes every command print one JSON document (for nimbus-privd).
#
# Why:  spec section 4.4 and docs/PLAN.md NOTE-33, NOTE-34, NOTE-35, NOTE-38.
#       The Control Center's privileged helper calls this tool instead of
#       containing its own apt logic; administrators can use it directly.
#       Python standard library plus python3-apt only.
#
# Exit status: 0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error, 75 busy (another apt or
#       update run holds a lock; the systemd unit retries later).
#
# Build values below are filled in from build/nimbus.conf when the package is
# built (tools/build-debs.sh); in the source they are placeholder tokens.
# Paths are module globals read at call time (never bound as default
# arguments), so tests can point them at a temporary directory.
# =============================================================================

